WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.060
Kostadis Roussos: Yay.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.250
Kostadis Roussos: Record.

3
00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:27.970
Kostadis Roussos: Get food.

4
00:01:48.130 --> 00:01:48.769
Thomas Kolivakis: Go ahead.

5
00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:49.630
Kostadis Roussos: promise.

6
00:01:49.630 --> 00:01:50.610
Nicholas Roussos: Yo…

7
00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.330
Thomas Kolivakis: blue.

8
00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:55.429
Kostadis Roussos: Did you… did you see… did you see Calmer's Quest log?

9
00:01:55.870 --> 00:01:58.260
Thomas Kolivakis: Alright, I haven't read it yet.

10
00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:01.030
Nicholas Roussos: I saw that you both did it, I didn't look at it yet.

11
00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.110
Kostadis Roussos: It's on the… you should see how it ends.

12
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.340
Kostadis Roussos: In the Discord chat.

13
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.180
Thomas Kolivakis: Okay.

14
00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:31.250
Thomas Kolivakis: I think the comma might be a bit lost.

15
00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:42.069
Kostadis Roussos: I… I… I was… I… I was… I like that. That captures Calmer's current state of mind.

16
00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:48.150
Kostadis Roussos: But, if you read the opening, Carrie, you'll see what…

17
00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:49.910
Kostadis Roussos: Your brother joining us?

18
00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:51.060
Thomas Kolivakis: Easier.

19
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.170
Kostadis Roussos: Oh, you did? Oh, George. Hey, Thomas. Hey, George, rather. All right.

20
00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:05.720
Kostadis Roussos: Gentlemen, we did not survive for prophets. A temple war, a wrath, trolls…

21
00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:24.110
Kostadis Roussos: a living pool, and several administrative meetings to throw away the first position of genuine authority any of us held. We will restore the supply line, secure the asset, learn what the deeper powers are hiding, and then, once the inventory is complete, make a properly informed decision about what, if anything, must be brought down.

22
00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.570
Kostadis Roussos: Calmer's, quest log.

23
00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.110
Kostadis Roussos: Okay, now let me just do something else.

24
00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:37.900
Kostadis Roussos: There we go.

25
00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.100
Kostadis Roussos: Okie dokie…

26
00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:50.770
Kostadis Roussos: Let me just read the summary.

27
00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:23.490
Kostadis Roussos: Alright.

28
00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:32.879
Kostadis Roussos: Four prisoners were still chained somewhere in the temple, and the party had left them without food for several days. When they finally reached the holding area, they found the chains torn apart and the captives got.

29
00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:47.179
Kostadis Roussos: An investigation check of 22 revealed that they had not escaped. Their corpses had been claimed by the necromancer and added to his growing arsenal of the dead. The necromancer's activities were becoming increasingly irritating, and the party resolved to track him down.

30
00:05:47.180 --> 00:06:02.360
Kostadis Roussos: Zephyr proposed posting notices throughout the temple, ordering anyone with information about the Necromancer to report to the party. Calmer enthusiastically approved. I think that's a fantastic idea, Zephyr. As the Chief of Staff, I think you're responsible for all matters related to security operations.

31
00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:16.759
Kostadis Roussos: Produce an appropriate note, and I will sign it. He then reconsidered and asked whether the initiative should probably belong to Zinnia as Chief of security. Sequoia, meanwhile, was reminded that he was in charge of supplies, or in his own words, I'm in charge of getting shit done.

32
00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:26.909
Kostadis Roussos: With Zinnia's approval, Calmer instructed Zephyr to bring him something to sign. Rather than immediately returning to their office, the party chose to finish exploring the remaining sections of the domain.

33
00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:46.590
Kostadis Roussos: Sequoia declared, I'm a completionist, and led them west, into a refuse-feld chamber that had once been a secluded place of relaxation. It was now heaped with rotting garbage, dung, bones, and skulls, with parts of a bronze-bound coffer visible near the center. Concerned that the necromancer would use the remains, the party decided to burn the entire room.

34
00:06:46.690 --> 00:06:57.569
Kostadis Roussos: No one had a suitable fire spell. Calmer admitted this was a mistake, and laughed when Zephyr asked about Meteor Storm. So Zephyr and Sequoia headed to the Fire Temple, while Zinnia stayed behind to keep an eye on Calmer.

35
00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:06.880
Kostadis Roussos: Taking an unexpected dark corridor on the way, they emerged into familiar territory. Offered the choice of approaching Vurakhal directly, they went instead to the captain of the card.

36
00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.570
Kostadis Roussos: Captain Varek Solain.

37
00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:22.899
Kostadis Roussos: Varek Solain, no longer defeated in demeanor, offered them and confirmed that the Refuse's room was where the Fire Temple habitually dumped its garbage. When told that a necromancer was quietly taking control of skeletons, he finally connected the threat to an old political grievance.

38
00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:29.760
Kostadis Roussos: The necromancer had served under Barkinar and disappeared after Romag removed the promotion he believed should have been his.

39
00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:45.209
Kostadis Roussos: Varek did not know where the necromancer was hiding, or even whether he remained inside the temple, but insisted that if undead were appearing, he's around. Varek had warned Alrrem about the danger, but Alrrem had ignored him, instead of finding the necromancer and making an alliance.

40
00:07:45.320 --> 00:08:04.719
Kostadis Roussos: Zephyr pressed Varek to find the necromancer, only for the captain to answer, with what army? I need supplies. I need food. I need troops. Nothing that the party had ta- noting that the party had taken his money and resources. Yes, Sequoia, as head of logistics, to send someone to Nulb and repair the supply chain. In the meantime, he provided several fire arrows and explained their use.

41
00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:20.850
Kostadis Roussos: Throw a flask of oil at the target, and then shoot it with a burning arrow. He stressed that his supply was limited. Offered the fire arrows, or Vurakhal's help with the burning. Zephyr took the arrows. The party turned around, routed around their own salamander retainer a second time.

42
00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:32.010
Kostadis Roussos: Zephyr then granted the Fire Temple control over the northern food depot. Varek was visibly delighted. Food is always a good thing. He who controls food controls everything.

43
00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:37.730
Kostadis Roussos: Zephyr immediately corrected, we control the food, not you. You're simply guarding it.

44
00:08:37.730 --> 00:08:53.249
Kostadis Roussos: Varek accepted this distinction, saying it demonstrated trust in the Fire Temple, but could not resist proclaiming, and fire shall burn again! Zephyr responded, Okay, maybe don't, and suggested placing an Earth Temple infiltrator nearby to keep the Fire Temple in check.

45
00:08:53.420 --> 00:09:00.040
Kostadis Roussos: When the party returned and set the refuge ablaze, a horrific creature emerged from the trash and furiously tied

46
00:09:00.230 --> 00:09:16.059
Kostadis Roussos: tried to douse the flames. The party chose to defend its territory rather than walking away. Calmer cost hold monster, successfully paralyzing the creature. Zinnia struck it repeatedly for automatic critical hits, Zephyr dealt 52 points in a devastating sneak attack, and Sequoia rolled

47
00:09:16.060 --> 00:09:28.720
Kostadis Roussos: 12 damage dice on a critical, only to average poorly and curse Frostbrand for having one job. The creature remained paralyzed through its saving throws. Calmer cast Toll of the Dead, and proudly remark, this new spell of mine is very effective.

48
00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:43.610
Kostadis Roussos: Zephyr eventually landed another 57-point critical and killed the creature. The party stepped outside and allowed the refuge chamber to burn for several hours. Continuing onwards, they found another room filled with broken containers whose disturbed litter showed recent traffic.

49
00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:57.730
Kostadis Roussos: Probably from carrying off the remaining foodstuffs. The temple's food supplies were plainly running low, and nobody was currently managing them. Beyond that lay an oddly shaped chamber packed with jars, boxes, barrels, crates, chests, sacks, casks, bales, bags, and hampers.

50
00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:07.339
Kostadis Roussos: Some were broken or empty, but many remained full. Bales had a black cloth and finished garments. Zinnia's inside roll of 25. Identified these as supplies.

51
00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:20.380
Kostadis Roussos: And uniforms belonging to the greater temple. The party's Arcana checks failed to reveal anything further. Sequoia nevertheless looked up, explaining, the answer is always on the ceiling. An investigation result of 21 vindicated him.

52
00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:39.310
Kostadis Roussos: Four creatures hung overhead by their tails. Clay's claws paused. I was right, Sequoia said in belief. I was saying a joke. Oh my god, the creatures were nightmarish, gaunt, ape-like predators with ash gray hides, four long, muscular arms ending in hooked black claws, powerful jaws, filled with uneven fangs.

53
00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:50.250
Kostadis Roussos: Three alert eyes and thick, prehensile tails wrapped around the stonework. Their limbs were unnaturally jointed for climbing, ambushing, and faint violet psychic energy pushed around their skulls.

54
00:10:50.250 --> 00:11:14.650
Kostadis Roussos: Zephyr acted first, but missed both pistol shots. Zinnia and Sequoia concentrated their attacks on the same creature, while the predators unleashed psychic blasts against the party. Zinnia, Zephyr, and Calmer resisted. Sequoia failed the DC-17 Wisdom save, suffered 17 points of damage, and was stunned. Guardians, creating a 15-fort aura that damaged and slowed several attackers.

55
00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:19.809
Kostadis Roussos: Thus, Zephyr's next pistol attack, including a sneak attack, damaged killed the wounded predator.

56
00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:35.689
Kostadis Roussos: The others swarmed Calmer with as many five claw attacks apiece, but his armor class of 21, bolstered by it, the new shield plus one, allowed only one blow through. He suffered 8 slashing damage and lost concentration on Spirit Guardians, while another creature missed him 5 times in succession.

57
00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:41.910
Kostadis Roussos: Calmer healed Sequoia after the wounded logistics chief plunged… pointedly suggested that the cleric could save him.

58
00:11:41.910 --> 00:12:00.379
Kostadis Roussos: Then used word of radiance against the enemies clustered around him. Zinnia slew a second creature, while Calmer continued alternating healing and radiant blasts. Are you okay, Sequoia? he asked, when Sequoia answered, I guess. Calmer replied, My guess is not an answer, yes or no. Sequoia finally answered, maybe, and morbed.

59
00:12:00.390 --> 00:12:09.190
Kostadis Roussos: Just don't blame me when your logistics breaks down. Calmer cast another healing ward, restoring 14 points, then struck both nearby predators with another word of presence.

60
00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:14.470
Kostadis Roussos: Word of Radiance. Zephyr used Chill Touch against one survivor, preventing it from regaining hip points.

61
00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:35.449
Kostadis Roussos: While Zinnia newly reminded of his stunning strike technique, and Sequoia continued the assault. The two remaining predators finally disengaged and fled to the shadowed corner. Zephyr warned them, you know where the boss is, okay, so don't ever try to anything again. He then tried to undercommon the one relevant tongue he has. No one in the party had deep speech, which is what these aberrations would have answered to.

62
00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:39.809
Kostadis Roussos: The creatures merely sneered, howled, hissed, and crawled into the darkness.

63
00:12:39.810 --> 00:12:49.980
Kostadis Roussos: And an exhausted and flustered Dren Halveth arrived shortly afterward, notepad in hand, delivered a perfectly deadpan summary of the temple's cascading of administrative disasters.

64
00:12:49.980 --> 00:13:02.310
Kostadis Roussos: Addressing Zephyr, he said, I've been doing the supply check. The Minotaur has food for three days. The men have pay for four. The dead have started leaving without permission. I can solve any one of these. I cannot solve all three while pretending this is a normal command.

65
00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:19.440
Kostadis Roussos: Dren explained that the supplies ordinarily came through Nulb, meaning some would have to travel there and restore the supply chain. The party issued its orders, signed the armor depot to the water temple, assigned the firewood depot to the air temple, burned corpses before the Necromancer could claim them, and feed usable bodies to the Minotaur.

66
00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:28.960
Kostadis Roussos: Dren requested permission to use the Fire Temple Salamander to help with the burning, and the party agreed. He also reminded them that Barkinar was still waiting for a decision about the Chest of Rao.

67
00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:42.330
Kostadis Roussos: The group resolved to travel to Nulb the following morning. Dren was left with broad authority to keep order, and the Minotaur fed, though Sequoia warned him, We trust you, but if you betray that trust, you know. They retired to their quarters, while Calmer relaxed, with satisfaction.

68
00:13:42.660 --> 00:14:00.359
Kostadis Roussos: And admitted, I like being in charge. That evening, as the party drank and rested, an illusory image of a hooded man appeared. Forgive the theatrics, he began. I cannot be seen as a single runner, and you cannot be afforded to be seen receiving one. The figure's message and the party's previous knowledge identified him through implication as phleranth.

69
00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:14.229
Kostadis Roussos: A wizard hiding from the greater temple, whom Barkinar had considered important enough to mention. Falrinth warned them about Lucius Graeme. The flattery man has already been to you, golden eyes, a soft hand, a great deal of wine. He gave you presents and asked.

70
00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:26.389
Kostadis Roussos: You what you were short of. Lucius Graeme. Write that name down. He collects the ones he gives you. Lucius had already visited the party carrying gifts, and Falrinth advised them not to commit when he returned, but to stall him.

71
00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:34.929
Kostadis Roussos: Falrinth then revealed that he possessed the Orb of Golden Death. The orb, this temple of frets over, yes, I have it. I'm not giving it to Hedrack nor to Senshock.

72
00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:45.100
Kostadis Roussos: nor to any of the holy gentlemen who would like me dead, I'm not giving it to you either. But that is a separate conversation. When Sequoia asked how he had acquired it, Falrinth responded.

73
00:14:45.100 --> 00:15:00.840
Kostadis Roussos: That is a convention conversation for another year. Romag had already previously described the fully assembled orb as a source of tremendous power, capable of submarining monsters and destroying virtually anything, raising the question of why Falrinth possessed it, but did not appear to be using it.

74
00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:12.530
Kostadis Roussos: Falrinth next turned his attention to Calmer Scarab and scribe TZGY. Yes, you should be far more careful with what you… that with it than you have been. Lucius will note on sight.

75
00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:18.239
Kostadis Roussos: Sunshark will know it on site. They will use it against you in different ways, and neither will tell you any notice.

76
00:15:18.240 --> 00:15:29.060
Kostadis Roussos: He also revealed that Lareth had been his friend, and said, I'm told you handled him with discretion, which I appreciate more than you would expect, but there are other friends, and not all of them are as patient as I am.

77
00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:46.939
Kostadis Roussos: Falrinth explained how to reach them. A candle in the west wall will reach me. Reporting him to Barkinar was another option, but Falrinth predicted that Barkinar would believe the party, and simply fail to find the wizard where they claimed he was. Either decision would reveal the party's choice of allegiance. As the illusion began to fade, Falrinth

78
00:15:47.060 --> 00:16:03.650
Kostadis Roussos: delivered his most chilling revelation. There is a room below, deep forgotten, on the level beneath your feet. The holy gentleman keeps something in it, a sleeper. My leash is short, and the gates are watch. But you, you have keys I never had. If you ever want Verbobonc and all its banners to come down on this terrible

79
00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:15.389
Kostadis Roussos: Hell, on this temple, Ado, you would find… you would come for this. Wake that what sleeps in the iron coffin. Ask your golden friend what he's so afraid of. You'll… so afraid, you'll find, then signal me.

80
00:16:15.390 --> 00:16:35.089
Kostadis Roussos: Only after trying to question him did the party realize that the projection was a one-way message whose creator had merely anticipated some of their likely responses. It faded away, leaving the party with the revelation that Falrinth either possessed the Orb of Golden Death, or was lying about it, and that something beneath their party could provoke a full military response for Verbobonc.

81
00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:39.420
Kostadis Roussos: The next… Morning, the party traveled to Nulb, dressed discreetly, choosing

82
00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:52.689
Kostadis Roussos: not to announce their new status as Lords of the Temple. Zephyr summarized their philosophy as power and subtlety. Calmer proved, good choice. That is why I've made you Chief of Staff. Zephyr added, we don't have to say that we're powerful, we just know.

83
00:16:52.690 --> 00:17:12.309
Kostadis Roussos: Prompting Calmer to puff himself up and answer, We just know. I like it. Smoke lay over the river, the same barges leaned against the same rotting pier, and men at the tavern doors continued arguing over which elemental would win a war that had ended beneath their feet 10 days earlier. Nulb but not change, which was how the party knew nobody had told it.

84
00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:19.579
Kostadis Roussos: On the first muddy stretch of the road, a Rhennee child from the riverfolk that had previously aided recognized them and ran shouting.

85
00:17:19.589 --> 00:17:30.830
Kostadis Roussos: Family has returned! As they entered the village, a dockhand pressed a folded note into Sequoia's palm. It read, Skole says, The captain is still telling people you're dead. He thought you might enjoy the update.

86
00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:40.689
Kostadis Roussos: Captive Tolub, who had previously tried to kill them, remained convinced, or wanted everyone else convinced that the party was dead. The game, it seemed, was far from over.

87
00:17:41.710 --> 00:17:42.660
Kostadis Roussos: Alright.

88
00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:50.850
Kostadis Roussos: Let's, get into Roll 20. Everybody in Roll 20? I'm not in Roll 20.

89
00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:11.150
Kostadis Roussos: Just to remind you a little bit, because it's been a while. Verbobonc? Okay, that was the end of the summary. Verbobonc…

90
00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.330
Kostadis Roussos: is…

91
00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:17.970
Kostadis Roussos: Which is tough.

92
00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:21.130
Kostadis Roussos: Put you guys on the map. Alright.

93
00:18:23.230 --> 00:18:26.429
Kostadis Roussos: So… Just a reminder.

94
00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:41.269
Kostadis Roussos: Verbobonc, this is the regional area that is in control of the borderland that encompasses Hommlet. Can you see the words Verbobonc?

95
00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:43.270
Thomas Kolivakis: Yep.

96
00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:44.710
Kostadis Roussos: Right.

97
00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:52.089
Kostadis Roussos: Hommlet is over here, and Nulb of is… well, Hommlet is over here. Verbobonc is this little tiny territory…

98
00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:58.749
Kostadis Roussos: It's essentially a sub-territory of the Archclericy of Veluna, which is a…

99
00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:04.740
Kostadis Roussos: region ruled by, the clerical order of St. Cuthbert.

100
00:19:08.400 --> 00:19:14.760
Kostadis Roussos: So… The kingdom of Furyondy is to the north, the city of Greyhawk is to the west.

101
00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:18.730
Kostadis Roussos: And we are back in nulled. Alright?

102
00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.210
Kostadis Roussos: Just get to know.

103
00:19:26.540 --> 00:19:28.460
Kostadis Roussos: Where's an old? I have an old.

104
00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:35.979
Kostadis Roussos: There we go.

105
00:20:00.930 --> 00:20:01.900
Kostadis Roussos: Alright.

106
00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:08.089
Kostadis Roussos: Okay, you guys can see each other. You see your souls, you've… Arrived into town.

107
00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:21.260
Kostadis Roussos: And as you arrive into town, actually… Let's move this.

108
00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:26.689
Kostadis Roussos: This is where the events start to occur.

109
00:20:28.890 --> 00:20:34.609
Kostadis Roussos: Alright? The, little kid, notices you, the,

110
00:20:38.140 --> 00:20:43.900
Kostadis Roussos: The, and you get the notice about Tolub.

111
00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:47.050
Thomas Kolivakis: I'll do it.

112
00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:50.749
Kostadis Roussos: But… and just remember, Tolub is the guy who sent you

113
00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:54.649
Kostadis Roussos: And the dust sent you to get killed by,

114
00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:59.109
Kostadis Roussos: By… remember those three clerics with the fireballs?

115
00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:03.480
Kostadis Roussos: Right.

116
00:21:04.190 --> 00:21:06.269
Kostadis Roussos: He's been bragging that you're dead.

117
00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:07.099
Kostadis Roussos: Or do you know…

118
00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:08.300
Thomas Kolivakis: where he is.

119
00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:14.230
Kostadis Roussos: Well, you know that he usually is in the Boatman's Tavern.

120
00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.520
Thomas Kolivakis: Do we confronted?

121
00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:21.489
Kostadis Roussos: Well, it's up to you to do what you want.

122
00:21:22.230 --> 00:21:27.779
Kostadis Roussos: The other thing… the other thing is that you got a note from the Rhennee folk.

123
00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:33.960
Kostadis Roussos: Right? And remember, you helped their doc… they helped the Eryk Velkori… Eryk's,

124
00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:39.520
Kostadis Roussos: what's the word I'm looking at what? Velkori,

125
00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:43.190
Kostadis Roussos: They offered you, you saved his daughter.

126
00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:51.890
Kostadis Roussos: So, you could also go and, you know, they could be potential allies, so visiting them is also an option.

127
00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:56.590
Kostadis Roussos: And they're viewed… and they view you as family, which is a big deal.

128
00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:04.219
Thomas Kolivakis: Well… I think we should go inform ourselves with the… the family.

129
00:22:04.610 --> 00:22:06.120
Kostadis Roussos: You gonna go with the family first?

130
00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:07.259
Thomas Kolivakis: To check out.

131
00:22:07.440 --> 00:22:09.419
Thomas Kolivakis: What the village thinks of us.

132
00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:17.270
Kostadis Roussos: Okay, so you're gonna go do that.

133
00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:19.530
Kostadis Roussos: Great.

134
00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:36.520
Kostadis Roussos: Great. So, okay, so you're gonna go visit… you're gonna go to the Rhennee, right?

135
00:22:44.650 --> 00:22:45.480
Kostadis Roussos: Right.

136
00:23:03.950 --> 00:23:09.100
Kostadis Roussos: As you're walking by, the various buildings.

137
00:23:09.990 --> 00:23:12.190
Kostadis Roussos: Including this one over here.

138
00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:24.599
Kostadis Roussos: You notice I… now, the Boatman's Tavern is where Tolub usually hangs out. Do you want to try to avoid going past it, or…

139
00:23:24.950 --> 00:23:26.760
Thomas Kolivakis: It's discrete, will be discrete.

140
00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:28.699
